# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# sizjobs .gitignore
# This repo is public. .gitignore prevents accidents; gitleaks
# (pre-commit and CI) and GitHub push protection catch the rest.
#
# CI (.github/workflows/tracked-files.yml) fails if any tracked file
# matches a pattern here, so `git add -f` cannot sneak one in.
# A file that really must be committed needs a `!` exception here,
# reviewed in a PR, not a forced add.
#
# Pattern syntax reminder:
#   foo      matches foo at any depth
#   /foo     matches only at the repo root
#   foo/     matches directories only
#   !foo     re-includes something an earlier pattern excluded
#            (does not work if a parent directory is excluded)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets and credentials: never committed --------------------
# Locally secrets live in ~/.config/sizjobs/.env, on AWS in SSM.
# Any copy inside the repo is a mistake.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
# direnv, netrc and PyPI configs often hold tokens in plain text
.envrc
.netrc
.pypirc
# Private keys and keystores (cosign.key matches *.key; cosign.pub is fine)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# Root-level scratch folder for anything secret
/secrets/
# Cloud and cluster credentials
.aws/
credentials.json
token.json

# --- Kubernetes, k3d, Helm ----------------------------------------
# kubeconfig contains client certs/tokens for the cluster.
# k3d writes one with `k3d kubeconfig write`; never copy it here.
kubeconfig*
*.kubeconfig
.kube/
# Secret manifests generated locally, e.g.
#   kubectl create secret generic x --from-env-file=... --dry-run=client -o yaml
# hold base64 (not encrypted) values. Helm chart templates named
# secret.yaml contain no values and are allowed back in.
secret.yaml
secrets.yaml
*-secret.yaml
*-secrets.yaml
*.secret.yaml
!**/templates/*secret*.yaml
# `helm dependency build` downloads subcharts as tarballs; Chart.lock
# is committed instead so the build is reproducible.
**/charts/*.tgz

# --- MinIO (local stand-in for S3) --------------------------------
# Local data directory if MinIO runs with a host bind mount, and the
# `mc` client config, which stores access and secret keys.
/minio-data/
.mc/

# --- Personal data: lives in the private bucket (MinIO, later S3) --
profile.yaml
companies.yaml
/private/
# Raw email exports. Only sanitized fixtures under tests/fixtures/ are committed.
/mail-raw/
*.eml
*.mbox
*.msg
!**/tests/fixtures/**/*.eml
# CVs, cover letters and job ads are usually PDF/Word. Outside docs/
# they are almost certainly personal.
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
!docs/**/*.pdf
# Local agent state (memory, caches) can contain personal data
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Terraform (.terraform.lock.hcl IS committed) -----------------
# Provider plugins and module cache, re-downloaded by `terraform init`
.terraform/
# State holds every resource attribute, including secrets, in plain text.
# Real state lives in the S3 backend.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
# Saved plans embed variable values (and so secrets)
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Override files are for local experiments only
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
# tfvars can hold secrets; commit only examples
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
# Terraform CLI config can contain API tokens
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# --- Python (uv) ---------------------------------------------------
# uv.lock and .python-version ARE committed: they pin the exact
# dependency set and interpreter. Only the venv and caches are ignored.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.tox/
.nox/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Evals (promptfoo) ----------------------------------------------
# Run results can include model output about the real profile.
evals/output/
.promptfoo/
# promptfoo is an npm package; a local install creates node_modules
node_modules/

# --- Local runtime data at the repo root only (a code folder named models/ is fine)
/models/
/.local/
*.log

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------
# Shared VS Code recommendations/settings are committed, the rest is personal
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Windows adds these alternate-stream files when copying into WSL
*:Zone.Identifier

# --- Claude Code ------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/settings.json, .claude/commands/ and .mcp.json ARE committed.
# .mcp.json must reference secrets as ${ENV_VAR}, never literal values.
# Personal, machine-local settings and notes:
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
# Git worktrees Claude Code creates for isolated sessions
.claude/worktrees/
